        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Update Learn fundamental layout comprehension]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41362</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41362"/>
        <updated>2025-10-01T12:37:22.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This PR is part of a series in which I update the Learn area "Challenge" articles. In general, they need to be modernized, restructured, and put in better positions in the modules so they are spaced out better and test subjects that have already been covered.</p>
<p dir="auto">In this PR specifically, I update the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/CSS_layout/Fundamental_Layout_Comprehension" rel="nofollow">Fundamental layout comprehension</a> challenge to:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Improve the HTML, CSS, and JS code in general.</li>
<li>Bring the article structure more in line with what I've been doing in other places, for example, consistent structure and reducing reliance on the learning-area repo</li>
<li>Moving the article to just after the grid content, as that means it sits just after the items it tests. I am intending to create a separate challenge to test some of these techniques combined with RWD (media queries, etc.)</li>
</ul>

